WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.460
Reflection can make trimming and Native AOT more difficult because build tools may not know which members must be preserved.

2
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.960
If code only names a type or member dynamically, static analysis may not see that dependency.

3
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:20.700
A member that exists during development can be missing in a trimmed or ahead-of-time deployment.

4
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.140
Reflection-heavy code should be minimized or isolated where possible.

5
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:33.720
A typed design, source-generated approach, explicit registry, or documented contract can make required members visible to tools and reviewers.

6
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:43.500
When reflection is needed, developers should make the required members explicit through analyzable patterns, attributes, source generation, or configuration that is reviewed.

7
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.820
Suppressing trim warnings should be a last resort after the reflection behavior is understood.

8
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.880
A warning may indicate that runtime behavior depends on members the build cannot prove are present.

9
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.540
The answer should not be to hide the warning before the team knows which feature depends on it.

10
00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.660
Library authors should communicate reflection requirements to callers.

11
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:11.560
Application developers need to know when a library expects certain constructors, properties, attributes, or methods to survive trimming.

12
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:20.060
Runtime failures caused by missing reflected members can affect authentication, authorization, validation, serialization, or diagnostics.

13
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.620
Deployment targets should be part of reflection design review.

14
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:35.320
A feature that works in a full framework-style deployment may need source generation, explicit metadata, or a different approach for trimmed, containerized, or Native AOT environments.
